 - `i18n/tools/update_strings.py` extracts menu text and the per-field table into the six catalogs.
+
+## Enhanced solar and lunar disc edges
+
+`src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/numos/numos_visible_discs.slangh` assembles the visible sky with the pinned
+NUMOS air, moon surface, stars and cloud LUTs. The camera composite and the PSR miss in
+`algorithm/geometry_resolver.slangh` use it. Diffuse and glossy gathers use the ordinary disk-free sky.
+`pass/numos/numos_disc.h` holds the rim and peak equations also checked by `test_enhanced_sky.cpp`.
+The emitted lights and the standalone library shaders keep their physical illuminance.
diff --git a/documentation/NumosSky.md b/documentation/NumosSky.md
index 250e5e012..1b72964e7 100644
--- a/documentation/NumosSky.md
+++ b/documentation/NumosSky.md
@@ -72,6 +72,13 @@ A miss skips the depth-based fog. In the paused policy, surface consumers see em
 
 The sun and moons are distant lights, so their disks appear only on paths that no light sample follows.
 
+The visible Sun and Moon use the same disc evaluator in the camera and a perfect mirror. Its rim spans
+two traced pixels, with NUMOS's two-percent angular floor at high magnification. The solar centre
+reaches at most 48 times the solar illuminance before atmospheric attenuation. Each moon has its own
+limit relative to its phase-dependent illuminance. The pinned lunar shader still samples the lunar
+surface at the real pixel footprint. Both the translucent lunar limb and the solid disc mask the
+Sun and stars behind them. The screen clouds cover the camera sky and the cloud dome covers a PSR miss.
+
 | Path | Disks | Indirect scale |
 |---|---|---|
 | Primary ray, drawn in the composite | Yes | No |
